keywords:
  - quiver mutation
  - cluster algebras
  - mutation equivalence
  - exchange graphs
  - forks
  - computer-assisted proof
abstract: >-
  How high must a mutation path between two quivers of small height climb?
  Four-vertex quivers of height b that reach their opposite only through
  height 2b^2 - 3b - 3 (even b, computer-assisted proof), five-vertex quivers
  of height t^2 that need 2t^5 - t^4 + t^2 - 1 (computer-assisted proof), and
  five-vertex quivers of height a + 1 that need about 4a^3 (exhaustive search
  for a <= 64, conjectured beyond). Also: Conjecture 5.5 of arXiv:2610.36179
  checked for every four-vertex quiver of height at most 18, and a census of
  788,026 four-vertex mutation classes. Notes, scripts, separately written
  checking scripts and the stored results. Produced with extensive help from
  AI tools; no human has read the paper.
